OL,3,GNEWSALong-serving Tory open to Reform
OL,4,Aco-operation
OL,5,
OL,6,FLong-serving Conservative MP Sir John
OL,7,FHayes has suggested his party could
OL,8,Fwork with Reform UK in the future,
OL,9,Fputting him at odds with Tory leader
OL,10,FKemi Badenoch.
OL,12,FHe said Reform UK were "not capable of
OL,13,Fgoverning on their own" but were "on
OL,14,Fthe same side" as the Conservatives "in
OL,15,Fterms of Labour".
OL,17,F"The possibilities of collaboration and
OL,18,Fcooperation are for the future," he
OL,19,Fsaid, during a Hotseat interview on BBC
OL,20,FRadio Lincolnshire.
OL,23,APub: 09-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
